//Multi-flag void method (AccessType NodeFlags KT_Void grammar variant):
//`public static void` requires the NodeFlags production — a single-flag
//rule alone would leave this shape a bare syntax error. The static flag is
//syntactic today (no static dispatch in the VM), so the method is invoked
//through an instance like any other method. Uses an out param for the
//observable effect instead of touching instance state from a static-flagged
//method.
class Util {
	public static void twice(int v, out int r) {
		r = v * 2;
	}
}

int main() {
	int r = 0;
	Util u = new Util();
	u.twice(21, out r);
	return r;
}
